Z||000000||JayUSA77||07-01-2001||03:31 PM||||Hey you guys now that i got must of my bugs out of my car i need to look into suspension packages.  I was told that KONI wore out in like a year and was not worth the high cost of 1000 dollars to replace all the time.  I need a better suspension kit that will be kick ass on the street for racing and just whipping doughnuts when im bored.  Also do you guys know where to get trailing arms to plant the tires down more firmly for less wheel hop.?????????? Help me out please.<BR>-J<BR><P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||07-01-2001||07:45 PM||||I had Koni Adjustables on my GTI VR6 for a couple years...they were still working fine when the car decided to self-destruct. <BR>(Fieros aren't the only cars to burst into flames...)<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||07-01-2001||09:24 PM||||Have them on my fiero<BR>Have them on the 87 Vette<BR>94 911<BR>and 2 corvairs <P>Love them , the corvair sets have been rebuilt 2 times in 20 years , and last checked they were still perfect.<P>The ones I have  on my fiero have been there for around 3 years , work great no problems , lots of track racing and autocrossing.<P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||07-01-2001||09:58 PM||||There's nothing wrong with the Koni's quality,although I wish the settings were more in tune with the needs of the Fiero;I've noticed that the people who have them tend to have the adjustments maxed out one way in the front,and the other in the rear,but as long as they work good that way,what the heck,huh?<BR>A swaybar will help out with the rear hop thing,a little,will still do it sometimes but not nearly as much.If your springs are tuned to work well without the use of a swaybar,a small diameter bar will still help it to ride a bit smoother as well fix part of the hop problem,and definately help out with the dreaded doughnut dillema.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||07-01-2001||10:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Have them on my fiero<BR>Have them on the 87 Vette<BR>94 911<BR>and 2 corvairs <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, how about some info on the Corvairs!  My dad has a '61 Monza 900 4-door be bought in 64.  Car's been awaiting a full-on restoration for longer than I care to remember, though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||07-01-2001||11:33 PM||||1966 Corvair Corsa (Canadian Built) you can tell a canadian corvair from others since it has a painted trunk instead of a Speckle finish<P>2.9ltr Flat 6 , Big valve heads , forged pistons 11:1 compression , 46 IDA downdraft tripple weber carbs. manifolds and heads extrude honded , lunati cam , 6 link rear suspension (aluminum) 3.55 gears , close ratio 4spd , koni's all around , sway bars, custom wound springs. Sparco race seats , 4 point harness , MSD 6AL ignition system ,balanced , poted polished. 2500lbs street weight , use to run SCCA CSP at 2021LBS. <P>The other is the identical car suspension wise (corbeau GT8 seats , no backseat in either car) This one has a 4.2ltr old aluminum block V8 , close ratio 4spd , 3.23 gears , crown heavy duty input shaft , custom made headers , lumati marine grind cam (motor runs backwards..firing order in reverse since thisis a rear engined V8) Motor weighs 320Lbs complete. 94.7 pt car at National Convention. <P><BR>Also have a 1969 Convert , garnet red , black interior , 140hp 4 carb motor , all original , original owner. 41,000 miles.<P>JM<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||10-01-2001||11:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Also have a 1969 Convert , garnet red , black interior , 140hp 4 carb motor , all original , original owner. 41,000 miles.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, old post, but I ran across it while doing a search and wanted to ask:<P>I thought 66 or 67 was the last year of the 140HP 4 carb motor?  I didn't think you get get anything other than the 2 carb motors in 69.  Is that right?  Maybe it was the turbo that was cancelled?  <P>I'd love to find a '66 Corsa 140, 4-speed convertible to play with, but then, who wouldn't?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||10-01-2001||01:08 PM||||66 was the last year for the 180hp turbo motor.<P>in 67 the 140 was not really available. But it has been found that some cars escaped from the factory with the 140<P>Not sure about 68 and 140 availability.<P>Our 69 is all original and has a 140 in it , it's not unusual to see a 69 140 , but it is rare. These motors were all smogged up unlike the 66 cars.<P>Other oddities , My grandfather had a 66 Corsa with a 140hp motor and a 3spd tranny. Wierd Wierd setup , not available as an option and should have never left the factory. I have also heard of 180Hp turbo cars with 3spd trannies off the floor.<P>No idea why..<P>All 521 converts in 69 were built by hand , no 2 cars are the same. Some of the gaps on the panels are "off" from the factory. and for some reason our factory decklid on the 69 convert measures a few mm shorter than our 66 decklid. (mold got worn?)<P>JM ||||reg||1
